.TH JOINPNGS 1 "October 11, 2026" "Vircon32 DevTools 26.04.24" "Vircon32 Development Tools"
.SH NAME
joinpngs \- pack a folder of PNG images into one texture image
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B joinpngs
.RB [ \-g
.IR gap ]
.RB [ \-hx
.BR left | center | right ]
.RB [ \-hy
.BR top | center | bottom ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.I input\-folder
.I output.png
.br
.B joinpngs
.B \-\-help
.br
.B joinpngs
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B joinpngs
loads every
.I .png
file in
.I input\-folder
(not in its subfolders) and arranges them, without overlapping, into
one image no larger than a Vircon32 texture (1024 by 1024 pixels),
written to
.IR output.png .
Drawing many images from one texture is much faster on the console
than switching between many small textures.
.PP
Next to the image it writes
.I output.xml
(the output path with its extension replaced), a project file for the
Vircon32 texture region editor (distributed separately). It describes
where each image ended up as a named region, with its hotspot; from the
editor, hotspots can be adjusted visually and C or assembly
definitions of the regions exported for a program to use with
.BR define_region (3v32).
.PP
Each region is named after its file, without the extension and with
spaces replaced by underscores. A file whose name ends with three
numbers,
.IB name _ columns _ rows _ gap .png\c
, is taken as a matrix of equally sized frames (an animation, a set of
tiles):
.I walk_4_2_1.png
is a grid of 4 by 2 frames separated by 1 pixel, with no border around
the grid. A matrix is kept in one piece and described in the XML as a
matrix of regions, which the editor and
.BR define_region_matrix (3v32)
understand.
.PP
Wider images are placed first (then taller, then by name). If the
images do not all fit in 1024 by 1024 pixels,
.B joinpngs
fails.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-g " gap"
Leave
.I gap
pixels (0 to 10, default 1) between neighboring images, so that scaled
or rotated drawing does not bleed pixels from one region into the next.
.TP
.BR \-hx " left|center|right"
Horizontal position of each region's hotspot in the XML (default
.BR left ).
.TP
.BR \-hy " top|center|bottom"
Vertical position of each region's hotspot in the XML (default
.BR top ).
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose: report each step.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and author, and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The image and the XML were written.
.TP
.B 1
Any error \(em an image larger than 1024 pixels on a side, a matrix
name whose numbers don't match the image size, images that don't fit
\(em printed as
.IR "joinpngs: error: description" .
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
joinpngs \-g 2 \-hx center \-hy bottom sprites/ obj/sprites.png
png2vircon obj/sprites.png \-o obj/sprites.vtex
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR png2vircon (1),
.BR packrom (1),
.BR video.h (3v32)
.SH AUTHOR
The Vircon32 PNG joiner was written by Javier Carracedo
